# Object.prototype takes no new name, so a definition under one throws in every run: the build stops. The literal of the descriptor is filled in front of the call, which runs no code of the program
# a definition that asks for what is already there succeeds, locked or not: nothing is said of it
# Object.defineProperty(Object.prototype, "w", { get() {} }); Object.defineProperty(Object.prototype, "toString", { writable: false });
# DIAGNOSTIC: LockedBuiltinWriteAlwaysRuns 1
# RUN: locks

